      "shell": "/usr/bin/osascript -l JavaScript -e 'var s1 = $.NSUserDefaults.alloc.initWithSuiteName(\"com.apple.applicationaccess\"); var s2 = $.NSUserDefaults.alloc.initWithSuiteName(\"com.apple.icloud.managed\"); var v1 = ObjC.unwrap(s1.objectForKey(\"allowFindMyDevice\")); var v2 = ObjC.unwrap(s1.objectForKey(\"allowFindMyFriends\")); var v3 = ObjC.unwrap(s2.objectForKey(\"DisableFMMiCloudSetting\")); var f1 = s1.objectIsForcedForKey(\"allowFindMyDevice\"); var f2 = s1.objectIsForcedForKey(\"allowFindMyFriends\"); var f3 = s2.objectIsForcedForKey(\"DisableFMMiCloudSetting\"); (v1 == false && v2 == false && v3 == true && f1 && f2 && f3) ? \"PASS\" : \"FAIL\"'"
    }
  },
  "discussion": "The Find My service _MUST_ be disabled.\n\nA device management solution _MUST_ be used to carry out remote locking and wiping instead of Apple's Find My service.\n\nApple's Find My service uses a personal AppleID for authentication. Organizations should rely on MDM solutions, which have much more secure authentication requirements, to perform remote lock and remote wipe.\n",
  "discussion_format": "asciidoc",
